6-.0425.0304.0486.0607 1.5482.1457.6618.0364h1.621l3.0175.2247.7892.522.4736.6376-.079.4857-1.2142.6193-1.6393-.3886-3.825-.9107-1.3113-.3279h-.1822v.1093l1.0929 1.0686 2.0035 1.8092 2.5075 2.3314.1275.5768-.3218.4554-.34-.0486-2.2039-1.6575-.85-.7468-1.9246-1.621h-.1275v.17l.4432.6496 2.3436 3.5214.1214 1.0807-.17.3521-.6071.2125-.6679-.1214-1.3721-1.9246L14.38 17.959l-1.1414-1.9428-.1397.079-.674 7.2552-.3156.3703-.7286.2793-.6071-.4614-.3218-.7468.3218-1.4753.3886-1.9246.3157-1.53.2853-1.9004.17-.6314-.0121-.0425-.1397.0182-1.4328 1.9672-2.1796 2.9446-1.7243 1.8456-.4128.164-.7164-.3704.0667-.6618.4008-.5889 2.386-3.0357 1.4389-1.882.929-1.0868-.0062-.1579h-.0546l-6.3385 4.1164-1.1293.1457-.4857-.4554.0608-.7467.2307-.2429 1.9064-1.3114Z"></path></svg>Ask in Claude</button></div></div><div aria-hidden="true" class="mt-1 h-px w-full bg-fd-border"></div></div></div><div class="prose docs-prose"><p>This page lists the Pyth contracts deployed on each supported chain. A chain can have three kinds:</p>
<div class="relative overflow-auto prose-no-margin my-6" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th>Contract</th><th>What it is</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Pyth Pro</td><td>Verifies the signed Pyth Pro price that each transaction carries, for use in that transaction. It stores no price.</td></tr><tr><td>Pyth Core</td><td>Verifies a signed update and stores the price, so any contract can read it until a newer update replaces it. The original Pyth Core contract, upgraded in place on August 26, 2026. Integrations kept their address.</td></tr><tr><td>Pyth Core Compatible</td><td>Stores prices like Pyth Core. A second Pyth Core contract with the same interface, deployed before the upgrade so integrations could upgrade early.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p><a href="/pro/use-prices-on-blockchain">Use Prices on Blockchains</a> explains how the Pyth Pro and Pyth Core contracts differ.</p>
<h2 id="solana" class="group/heading flex scroll-m-28 flex-row items-center gap-1"><a data-card="" href="#solana">Solana</a><button aria-live="polite" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md text-sm font-medium duration-100 disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-fd-ring hover:bg-fd-accent hover:text-fd-accent-foreground p-1 [&amp;_svg]:size-4 not-prose shrink-0 text-fd-muted-foreground opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover/heading:opacity-100"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-link" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg><span class="sr-only">Copy Anchor Link</span></button></h2>
<p>The Pyth Pro program has the same address on each Solana network:</p>
